msgid "REST end point validation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"While using the `Validator` manually might be useful for some advanced "
"usage,\n"
"if you simply want to validate the parameters or the return value or your "
"REST end point,\n"
"you can annotate it directly, either with constraints (`@NotNull`, `@Digits`."
"..)\n"
"or with `@Valid` (which will cascade the validation to the bean)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Let's create an end point validating the `Book` provided in the request:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As you can see, we don't have to manually validate the provided `Book` "
"anymore as it is automatically validated."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If a validation error is triggered, a violation report is generated and "
"serialized as JSON as our end point produces a JSON output.\n"
"It can be extracted and manipulated to display a proper error message."
msgstr ""

msgid "An example of such a report could be:"
msgstr ""

